        "text": "Radha is portrayed as an idealising figure of beauty, grace and sensitivity reflecting the concept of the \"uttam nayika\" in classic Indian literature. Radha has the pooja thali, the platter of flower, and sweetmeat near her, the ritual of worship and adulation to be completed before the love play starts.",
